{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Advances ONE accepted kb.plan item by REASONING about it via agent.llm.tool_loop, and CLOSES the loop on completion. The human move_item to `accepted` is the authorization; the item's claim+detail is the GOAL and the executive works out the means in one bounded tool_loop turn (TOOL_BUDGET rounds, self-checkpointing at the cap). Gate: only `accepted` entries eligible (the agent never self-promotes). CONVERGENCE GUARD: prior steps = step_log length; at/over MAX_PLAN_STEPS (default 20) it refuses with needs_reapproval until a human re-accepts via move_item. The model ends each turn with STATUS: DONE | IN_PROGRESS | BLOCKED; DONE requires a VERIFIED: evidence line (a concrete check it actually ran) or tool_loop parses it as IN_PROGRESS so an unverified claim can't close an item. On a verified DONE the item's `done` tag is applied in the SAME atomic journaled patch as the step_log (action completed, moved_to_done) - epistemic_work then drops it and the 15-min loop ENDS. BLOCKED surfaces once (action blocked) with the blocker carried into the next prompt. IN_PROGRESS continues under the budget. Re-checks source-pointer hash and defers to the stale path on drift. The bounded final answer (never the transcript) is journaled to step_log via patch_control_facet under base hash - on stale_base it aborts, never forces. base is the board hash from agent.plan.board. Returns action stepped|completed|blocked|step_failed|needs_reapproval|defer_stale|gated, loop_status, steps_taken/max_steps.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;","params":[{"name":"claim","type":"String"},{"name":"base","type":"String"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"opjijl1a158e0142bq1bd6","readers":[],"time":1792520512780,"username":"system","writers":[]}